# Node-RED API Rules

## CRITICAL: Deploy pattern (GET→POST, never PUT)

```
GET /flows (header: Node-RED-API-Version: v2)
→ returns {flows: [...], rev: "abc123"}

Modify node(s) in-place within the flows array

POST /flows (headers: Node-RED-API-Version: v2, Node-RED-Deployment-Type: full)
Body: {rev: "abc123", flows: [...modified flows...]}
→ returns {rev: "new-rev"}

On 409 → rev mismatch → retry with fresh GET
```

**NEVER** use `PUT /flow/:id` — it reorders tabs. This is the bug we're fixing.

## Flow structure
```
flows array contains:
├── Tab objects:     {id, type: "tab", label, info, disabled, order}
├── Node objects:    {id, type: "function"|..., name, z: "<tab-id>", wires: [[...]], ...}
├── Group objects:   {id, type: "group", name, z: "<tab-id>", nodes: ["node-id-1", ...]}
├── Subflow defs:    {id, type: "subflow", name, ...}
├── Subflow instances: {id, type: "subflow:<def-id>", z: "<tab-id>", ...}
└── Config nodes:    {id, type: "server"|..., z: "" (global) or "<tab-id>"}
```

## Key relationships
- **Node → Tab:** `node.z` = tab ID
- **Node → Group:** `group.nodes[]` contains node ID
- **Node → Node:** `node.wires` = array of arrays (one per output)
- **Config node scope:** `z = ""` means global, otherwise tab-scoped

## Context API (safe — read-only GET)
```
GET /flow/:id/context          → list all keys
GET /flow/:id/context/:key     → get specific key value
```
These endpoints are safe (read-only, no reorder risk).

## Function nodes
- Code in `node.func` field (JavaScript string)
- Init code in `node.initialize`
- Cleanup in `node.finalize`
- Output count in `node.outputs`

## Auth
- Basic Auth to port 1880 (direct Node-RED, not HA ingress)
- 401/403 → raise `NRAuthError`
- Always include `Node-RED-API-Version: v2` header on /flows endpoints

## Immutable fields on deploy
These fields MUST NOT be changed via `nr_safe_deploy`:
- `id` — node identity
- `type` — node type
- `z` — tab membership (moving nodes between tabs is not supported)
